      "incorrect": "He put off his hat at the door.",
      "correct": "He took off his hat at the door.",
      "note": "The opposite of **put on** a hat is **take off**; **put off** means to delay."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "I wore my hat and went outside.",
      "correct": "I put on my hat and went outside.",
      "note": "**Put on** is the action of getting dressed; **wear** describes having something on."
